avatar-proxy: separate avatar cache dir, serve only _avatar names, fixes F-007

From: Andy Green <andy@warmcat.com>

The shipped example conf pointed the avatar-proxy cache-dir at the
gitohashi JSON cache-base.  Since the avatar mount is unauthenticated
and serves <cache-dir>/<c>/<c>/<tail> for any clean-looking tail, raw
JSON cache entries (shape-identical names) were fetchable through it,
and repo-affiliated cache keys are unsalted and vhost-independent, so
a repo public on one vhost had its private-on-another-vhost views
computable cross-vhost.

- Give the avatar cache its own dir in both example confs and document
  that it must not equal cache-base.  The dir structure is prepared by
  avatar-proxy itself at INIT now (F-003).
- Pin the mount to the exact avatar filename shape, 32 hex chars +
  "_avatar", the only names it creates, so nothing else in a
  misconfigured shared dir is servable.
